@host = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@token = paste-a-valid-token-from-auth.http-here

### Create a task
POST {{api}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Buy milk",
  "description": "2% please"
}

### List my tasks
GET {{api}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get a single task
GET {{api}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a task - only what is sent is written
PATCH {{api}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Buy oat milk",
  "description": "the barista kind"
}

### Rename only - the description is left exactly as it was
PATCH {{api}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Buy oat milk"
}

### Clear the description - an empty title would be rejected instead
PATCH {{api}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "description": ""
}

### Set the status outright - repeating this changes nothing the second time
PATCH {{api}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "completed"
}

### Cycle status: created -> in_progress -> completed -> created
### Relative, so a retry after a lost response moves the task again.
POST {{api}}/tasks/1/toggle-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a task
DELETE {{api}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List with pagination
GET {{api}}/tasks/?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only the tasks in progress, oldest first
GET {{api}}/tasks/?status=in_progress&sort=created_at&order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sorted by title
GET {{api}}/tasks/?sort=title&order=asc&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
